            "a": "CIRRHOTIC HEPATORENAL SYNDROME with infection-triggered AKI + PARADOXICAL ELECTROLYTE DERANGEMENT: (1) Infection/peritonitis → splanchnic vasodilation → renal vasoconstriction (hepatorenal reflex) → AKI + oliguria, (2) Spironolactone (K-sparing) + oliguria + AKI → HYPERKALEMIA (K 5.2), (3) But SIMULTANEOUSLY hyponatremia from SIADH + cirrhosis (K paradoxically high DESPITE hyponatremia = very abnormal), (4) This indicates SEVERE renal failure; MANAGEMENT: (1) STOP spironolactone (worsening hyperkalemia in AKI context), (2) STOP furosemide (patient is volume-depleted from infection/vasodilation), (3) Aggressive fluid resuscitation with ALBUMIN (NOT crystalloid — plasma expansion needed in cirrhosis), (4) EMERGENCY DIALYSIS (for hyperkalemia + AKI management), (5) Antibiotics for SBP (cefotaxime), (6) Terlipressin (if available — vasopressor for hepatorenal syndrome), (7) ICU admission"
