            "q": "A 62-year-old with panhypopituitarism (on levothyroxine + hydrocortisone replacement) develops RESISTANT HYPONATREMIA (Na 109, SIADH pattern) despite fluid restriction + desmopressin held. He has history of temporal lobe epilepsy on CARBAMAZEPINE (known to cause SIADH). Additionally: he's found to have ADRENAL INSUFFICIENCY (cortisol 2, very low despite hydrocortisone replacement). What is the diagnostic TRAP?",
