            "rationale": "Polyendocrine failure creates LAYERED complications: (1) Central DI → needed desmopressin + free water, (2) Addison's → severe cortisol deficiency (cortisol needed for free water excretion + electrolyte regulation), (3) Thiazide → worsens BOTH hyponatremia (SIADH) + hyperkalemia (paradoxically increases K in Addison's), (4) Hypothyroidism → impairs free water clearance. Treatment priorities sequential: (1) Cortisol replacement (foundational — fixes many electrolyte issues), (2) Stop diuretic (causing dual electrolyte chaos), (3) DI management (desmopressin + free water with adequate cortisol), (4) Acute hyperkalemia management (dialysis if necessary). Prognosis: With prompt hydrocortisone + diuretic discontinuation, many electrolyte derangements resolve. Mortality high without recognition (adrenal crisis alone ~5-10% mortality if untreated)."
