            "a": "ACUTE MASSIVE PULMONARY EMBOLISM (PE) from deep vein thrombosis (DVT) post-op (orthopedic surgery high-risk for VTE) — EKG S1Q3T3 + RV strain pattern suggests massive PE with hemodynamic compromise; EMERGENCY: (1) STAT CT pulmonary angiography (CTPA) if time permits but consider treating empirically given clinical urgency (don't delay for imaging), (2) STAT troponin + BNP (RV strain assessment), (3) Unfractionated heparin bolus 80 units/kg IV IMMEDIATELY (anticoagulation while awaiting imaging), (4) Prepare for thrombolysis or catheter-directed thrombectomy (hemodynamically unstable PE = high-risk → consider aggressive intervention), (5) ICU admission, (6) Mechanical support (ECMO) if decompensates"
